Expected elements: present

All required elements render. The provenance banner sits first, above a slim identity bar carrying the exit to `aztec`, the truncated hash, `Partial`, block 101, both stepping directions, a scrubber, the `128 / 1315` readout and the FETCHING/OPENING/POSITIONING rail. Code is titled Code with line 32 unmistakably current; Call Trace and Event Log are one tab strip with Call Trace open and seven frames; Values is a separate pane below it, not a third tab; the Transaction pane carries identity. Nothing forbidden appears — no spinner, no empty pane, no full-width prose band below the banner, no light chrome. The three landed fixes read correctly: the capture is a true 1920x1080 with nothing clipped at the bottom, the `NOIR` tag is earned, and the cost row now reads `88000 / 200000 mana (FeeJuice)` with no dangling separator.

In my lens the page is competent and dense, but its numeric and truncation rules are not one rule. Thousands separators appear only in the call trace's opcode column; the same magnitudes elsewhere run unseparated. The same hash gets three treatments in the Transaction pane alone, two of them wrapping mid-byte. Code lines hard-clip mid-identifier with no ellipsis or scroll cue. And the disclaimer is the largest, loosest type on a tool surface — a hierarchy inversion that also costs the panes roughly 180 px.

Highest-priority fixes: one numeric formatter across every pane, and one hash truncation rule (middle-ellipsis, no wrapping).

Rating: 7/10

